cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Astronaut Trends: A reproducible analysis of global human-spaceflight participation, 1961–2026"
message: "If you use this dataset, software, or figures, please cite it as below, and credit the underlying Planet4589 source data."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Richard
    family-names: Barker
    affiliation: "AstroBotany Laboratory, University of Wisconsin–Madison; MadWest Rocketry"
abstract: >-
  Astronaut Trends is a reproducible data pipeline, published dataset, and
  interactive dashboard analysing six decades of human spaceflight. Drawing on
  Jonathan McDowell's General Catalogue of Astronauts (planet4589.org), it
  classifies every flown astronaut (1961–2026) by year of first flight,
  citizenship group (USA, Russia/USSR, China, Other), cumulative career duration
  in space (binned into five bands), and gender. The repository provides tidy
  machine-readable datasets, a Python reprocessing pipeline that can refresh the
  analysis from the primary source, static figures, and a self-contained
  interactive web dashboard with linked box-and-whisker, bar, sankey, chord,
  network, radar, heatmap and time-series visualisations.
keywords:
  - astronauts
  - human spaceflight
  - space history
  - data visualization
  - open data
  - reproducible research
  - space biology
  - commercial spaceflight
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dr-richard-barker/Astronaut_trends"
url: "https://dr-richard-barker.github.io/Astronaut_trends/"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-11"
references:
  - type: data
    title: "General Catalogue of Astronauts"
    authors:
      - given-names: Jonathan
        family-names: McDowell
    url: "https://planet4589.org/space/astro/lists/"
    notes: "Primary source for astronaut and mission records."
